# KSI-MLA-LET: Azure Activity Log Alert - Policy Assignment Changes
# CIS Azure 5.2.1: Alert on create/update policy assignment
# CIS Azure 5.2.2: Alert on delete policy assignment

META
    esp_id `ksi-mla-let-az-activity-alert-policy-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-MLA-LET: Azure Activity Alert - policy assignment write monitored`
    description `Validates that an activity log alert exists and is enabled to detect creation or modification of Azure Policy assignments, ensuring governance changes are tracked and communicated`
    author `security-team`
    tags `azure,activity-log,alert,policy,governance,CIS-5.2.1`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,NIST:AU-12,NIST:SI-4`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-LET`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `3`
    recommendation `Create activity log alert via az monitor activity-log alert create --name alert-policy-assignment-write --condition category=Administrative and operationName=Microsoft.Authorization/policyAssignments/write --action-group <ag-name>`

    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Event logging for governance changes is validated by confirming an activity log alert exists (found=true) and is enabled (enabled=true) that monitors the Administrative category for Microsoft.Authorization/policyAssignments/write operations. The alert must have at least one action group configured (has_action_groups=true) to ensure notifications are delivered when policy assignments are created or modified. Policy assignment changes can materially affect the security posture of the subscription and must be tracked.`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Changes to Azure Policy assignments are logged and monitored through activity log alerts that trigger on policyAssignments/write operations, providing real-time notification of governance modifications to the cloud service offering.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT alert_policy_write
        name `alert-policy-assignment-write`
        resource_group `rg-example-eastus`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE st_alert_active
        found boolean = true
        enabled boolean = true
        category string = `Administrative`
        operation_name string = `Microsoft.Authorization/policyAssignments/write`
        has_action_groups boolean = true
        action_group_count int >= 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_activity_log_alert
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF st_alert_active
            OBJECT_REF alert_policy_write
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
